Local persistence: the localStorage adapter.

The only module permitted to touch browser storage, on the same principle
that confines fetch to src/api/. This is the working-set store; files are the
interchange format and arrive with Milestone 5's JSON import/export.

Storage can be unavailable (private browsing) or full, and both surface as
errors rather than silence -- see .claude/CLAUDE.md on error handling. The editor
must stay fully usable when persistence is unavailable.

Reads go through ../serialization/. A stored document was written by some
build, not necessarily this one, so it is not trusted.

Empty until Milestone 3.
